      "code": "# Q2: Instance variables vs class/static variables\nclass Student:\n    college = \"LJCCA\"                 # class variable (shared by all objects)\n    def __init__(self, name):\n        self.name = name              # instance variable (unique per object)\n \ns1, s2 = Student(\"Janvi\"), Student(\"Disha\")\nprint(f\"{s1.name} studies at {s1.college}\")\nprint(f\"{s2.name} studies at {s2.college}\")\nStudent.college = \"L J College of Computer Applications\"   # changes for all\nprint(f\"After update -> {s1.name}: {s1.college}, {s2.name}: {s2.college}\")",
