      "logic": "The balance is kept as a name-mangled private attribute (<b>__balance</b>), only reachable through the class's own methods &mdash; a mutator (<b>set_balance</b>) writes it and an accessor (<b>get_balance</b>) reads it, which is the standard encapsulation pattern.",
      "code": "# Q3: Mutator and accessor methods\nclass Account:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.__balance = 0            # private instance variable\n \n    def set_balance(self, amount):    # mutator\n        self.__balance = amount\n \n    def get_balance(self):            # accessor\n        return self.__balance\n \nacc = Account()\nacc.set_balance(5000)\nprint(\"Balance via accessor:\", acc.get_balance())",
      "codeHtml": "<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"tok-com\"># Q3: Mutator and accessor methods</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> Account:</span><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">__init__</span>(self):</span><span class=\"line\">        self.__balance = <span class=\"tok-num\">0</span>            # private instance variable</span><span class=\"line\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">set_balance</span>(self, amount):    # mutator</span><span class=\"line\">        self.__balance = amount</span><span class=\"line\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">get_balance</span>(self):            # accessor</span><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"tok-kw\">return</span> self.__balance</span><span class=\"line\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"line\">acc = <span class=\"tok-fn\">Account</span>()</span><span class=\"line\">acc.<span class=\"tok-fn\">set_balance</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">5000</span>)</span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"tok-fn\">print</span>(&quot;Balance via accessor:&quot;, acc.<span class=\"tok-fn\">get_balance</span>())</span>",
