      "code": "# --- student.py (module) ---\n# student.py - Student class with mutator (set_) and accessor (get_) methods\nclass Student:\n    def set_id(self, id):       self.id = id\n    def get_id(self):           return self.id\n    def set_name(self, name):   self.name = name\n    def get_name(self):         return self.name\n    def set_marks(self, marks): self.marks = marks\n    def get_marks(self):        return self.marks\n \n \n# --- program using the module ---\n# Q7: Program using the Student class already defined in student.py\nfrom student import Student\n \ns = Student()\ns.set_id(21); s.set_name(\"Pruthvi\"); s.set_marks(91)\nprint(f\"ID: {s.get_id()}, Name: {s.get_name()}, Marks: {s.get_marks()}\")",
