      "code": "# Q15: Override the superclass method in the subclass\nclass Shape:\n    def area(self): print(\"Area not defined for generic shape\")\n \nclass Square(Shape):\n    def __init__(self, side): self.side = side\n    def area(self): print(\"Area of square:\", self.side ** 2)   # overridden\n \nShape().area()\nSquare(6).area()",
      "codeHtml": "<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"tok-com\"># Q15: Override the superclass method in the subclass</span></span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> Shape:</span><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">area</span>(self): <span class=\"tok-fn\">print</span>(&quot;Area <span class=\"tok-kw\">not</span> defined <span class=\"tok-kw\">for</span> generic shape&quot;)</span><span class=\"line\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"tok-kw\">class</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">Square</span>(Shape):</span><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">__init__</span>(self, side): self.side = side</span><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"tok-kw\">def</span> <span class=\"tok-fn\">area</span>(self): <span class=\"tok-fn\">print</span>(&quot;Area of square:&quot;, self.side ** <span class=\"tok-num\">2</span>)   # overridden</span><span class=\"line\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"tok-fn\">Shape</span>().<span class=\"tok-fn\">area</span>()</span><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"tok-fn\">Square</span>(<span class=\"tok-num\">6</span>).<span class=\"tok-fn\">area</span>()</span>",
